            "notes": "All three ADMIT this, and that agreement is the finding. `$` tolerates at most one trailing newline in PCRE and Python and none in JavaScript, so a single trailing SPACE defeats the reservation everywhere — the surface names its tool `terminal_confirm ` and every language hands the confirmation tool to the agent. A cross-language suite cannot surface this by comparing languages, because there is nothing to compare; it is recorded here so the row goes RED the day someone closes it. See G-36.",
